"""MIT. Prepare the final five-section draft PR body from actual closing receipts."""
import json, subprocess
from pathlib import Path
r=Path('/workspace/v3d-r4-media');product=Path('/workspace/splashery-r4-public');media=Path('/workspace/splashery-r4-clips-public')
head=lambda p:subprocess.check_output(['git','rev-parse','HEAD'],cwd=p,text=True).strip()
product_sha=head(product);media_sha=head(media)
packet=media/'review/video-3d-r4/evidence/final-r12-report-r9'
summary=json.loads((packet/'summary.json').read_text());g=json.loads((packet/'gates.json').read_text())
review=json.loads((media/'review/video-3d-r4/reviews/candidate-r12-unranked-r9/capture/publication.json').read_text())
controls=json.loads((media/'review/video-3d-r4/evidence/r12-closing-controls-r9/capture/publication.json').read_text())
base='https://github.com/ryanjosephkamp/splashery/'
evidence=base+'tree/'+media_sha+'/review/video-3d-r4/'
blob=base+'blob/'+media_sha+'/review/video-3d-r4/'
fmt=lambda x:format(x,'.6g') if isinstance(x,(int,float)) else 'unavailable'
q=g['profiles']['phone'];desktop=g['profiles']['desktop']
lines=['## Summary','','Codex built it. Adds a licensed 20-clip Video to 3D benchmark and improves new bakes with supported surface detail, robust seed bounds, bounded software raster work, validation-constrained environment color, and recovery from optional finishing failures. Engine changes remain in separate `Engine:` commits.','','The final native capture does not establish the complete goal. This PR stays a draft, with the run bounded to twelve hours. The native candidate is frozen at `64ec9ad5b7a90b590b289f6a02f0bbd50138db08`; the branch normally merged main `cb8a8315` and retains identical Video to 3D module, pack, and splatjs bytes.','',f'[Audit]({base}blob/{product_sha}/docs/audits/video-3d-r4-2026-10.md) · [Closing native evidence]({blob}evidence/final-r12-report-r9/CLOSING-INDEX.md) · [Media and licenses]({evidence})','','## Verification','',f"- Final capture: {summary['mainRows']}/40 main rows, {summary['pairedMasterRows']}/40 strict paired rows, all {summary['rawAttempts']} raw reservations, and all forty declared cases visible. Strict phone quality has {q['pairedMeasurable']} comparable pairs: diagnostic median sharpness ratio {fmt(q['sharpnessGain'])} and SSIM median change {fmt(q['ssimGain'])}. These are incomplete-subset diagnostics, not corpus acceptance. Desktop has {desktop['pairedMeasurable']} comparable quality pairs.",'- Both revision 12 and the separate app replay after merging main preserved all 74 held-out views across six samples and both profiles, with process exit zero and no recorded browser errors. Final reporting independently decoded both image sets against main. This verifies existing bakes and viewer behavior, rather than retraining samples.','- Focused revision-12 browser checks passed 66 cases, followed by seventeen product-wiring checks. Analytic and actual GPU controls cover constrained fitting, recovery, ownership, raster capacity, and unchanged default behavior. These counts overlap and are not a combined unique-test total.',f'- [Latest complete full CI]({base}actions/runs/38749424734): all sixteen original shards, 341 spec files, 2,920 tests, 2,914 passes, five failures, and one existing skip. Failures remain `spg:138`, `img-engine:85`, `man5:201`, `smoke:881`, and `live5:63`. None is a Video to 3D spec; all original failures still count. Original logs are retained.',f"- [Actual paired review]({blob}reviews/candidate-r12-unranked-r9/capture/README.md): {review['capturedClips']} source-bound verified phone movies. Only completed captures that pass exact replay and publication verification are advertised. Partial files and failures remain explicit.",'- All 285 original specs were byte-audited: 266 match task-start main, nineteen match normally merged main, and none was changed by this task. Tests are additive; no original assertion, threshold, or skip was weakened.','- Whole-repository Prettier and the unchanged English checker passed before pushes. Exact raw bytes are retained through original-path and SHA-256 restoration maps.','','## Deviations','','The host provides a four-core CPU quota and SwiftShader software graphics. Native jobs overlap host work; phone and desktop are viewport profiles. These observations do not establish isolated or physical-phone timing. The exploratory corpus also lacks a ground-level tabletop phone orbit and a busy pedestrian street.','',f"The separate 16:15 UTC baseline stage boundary recorded `stageInterrupted={str(controls['baselineStageInterrupted']).lower()}`; {len(controls['baselineTermSent'])} retained main identities received TERM and {len(controls['baselineKillSent'])} received KILL. Original per-case host parameters, benchmark rows, and scores were unchanged. Interrupted work stays incomplete. Review never owns timed bakes and ends by 16:31:30 UTC. The hard goal bound is October 15, 2026, at 16:32:25 UTC.",'','The original review watcher failed during process observation before capture. The actual R3 replacement retained all 262 historical bindings, added the postmerge sample controller, and passed all 80 CPU controls before authorization. Failed initial drafts and original errors remain in the closing controls.','','## Known issues','','Both-profile corpus quality, complete phone median/worst timing, and the every-clip outcome guarantee remain unproved. A dropped main success cannot earn a quality gain. The desktop baseline has no completed quality reconstruction. Full CI still has five failures.','',f"The ten-movie requirement is {'met for available strict phone pairs' if review['capturedClips']==10 else 'unmet'}; complete-corpus best/worst ranking remains unavailable. Movies are unranked and selected in manifest order, independent of score. They show synchronized replay, not device speed.",'','The plant phone pair is 14.050 times sharper, but loses 0.033142 SSIM and delays the first view. Other individual SSIM regressions and all harness errors remain recorded in the per-case tables; subset medians do not erase them.']
if review['preflightRejection']:
 lines+=['','Publication verification rejected the current review output or exceeded its closing CPU budget. Zero movies are advertised as verified, with original output and rejection preserved.']
lines+=['','## What was cut','','Direct and playback-assisted decoder experiments remain rejected because independent JPEG and presentation-time proofs did not all hold. Production extraction and held-out replay guards remain unchanged. Rejected geometry, depth, and loss experiments stay labeled diagnostics.','','Complete-corpus five-best/five-worst selection and physical-device timing require complete comparable measurements. Missing outcomes were not filled with invented models, favorable older attempts, or relaxed tests.','','Rule check: none.']
out=r/'pr-body-final-r9.md';assert not out.exists();out.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print(json.dumps({'body':str(out),'productHead':product_sha,'mediaHead':media_sha,'verifiedMovies':review['capturedClips'],'allGatesEstablished':False}))
